{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And He said, If you will diligently hearken.</b> I have already mentioned that every שמיעה followed by a lamed or bet does not mean to hear the thing, but rather to understand the reason of the matter that the statement concerns. And this שמיעה is to understand what commandment to do." "<b>And that which is upright in His eyes you shall do.</b> These are positive commandments." "<b>And give ear to His commandments.</b> Negative commandments, to consider what they are." "<b>And keep all His statutes.</b> That one not transgress them, as \"and you shall not walk in the statutes of the nations\" (Leviticus 20:23), and the statute of HaShem is that they not do like their deeds." "And the meaning of the disease. You have it to remember, for with your own eyes you saw the disease and the plagues and the smitings which I placed upon Egypt because they rebelled against Me. And if you heed My statutes, you will escape from them, for I will not do to you as I did to them. And furthermore, for I am YHWH your healer — from every disease that I decreed to exist upon the earth, you have no need for a physician, just as I healed the bitter waters, which no physicians have the power to heal. And behold, a bitter thing is the opposite of the first plague, for its waters were sweet and they could not drink them, and here the bitter waters — by means of it sweet ones were made. And behold, HaShem made the thing and reversed it upon you have it to beware lest you provoke it, and to love it, for it will do good to you."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {4 "The clause 'והפכו על יש לך' is textually difficult; it may be corrupt. Rendered hyper-literally as 'and reversed it upon you have it' to preserve whatever the underlying syntax intends without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:59.209532446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}